Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||09:40 AM||||I finally got around to fixing my stuck front caliper last night on my 85 SE, and its seized up good. I tried to twist the piston to free it up, guess what, that sucker is ceramic! (twisting the piston worked on my Saturn). Busted!<P>  So I hit PartsPlus this morning, expecting to shell out $150 or more for a new/rebuilt caliper. When the lady told me the price I almost fell off the customer stool.<P>  Minus the core charge: $35 !!!!!!!!<P> I couldnt believe it! Almost tempted to replace both of them<P>  I had her check the rear ones. One loaded with the brake pads is $95.<P>  Everytime i work on this car I like it more and more.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||05-04-2001||12:41 PM||||thats why i said 'why bother' Ken. for $70 you have 2 brand new ones, on the road in 1/2 hour, usually with a lifetime guarantee. to me anyway, its just not worth the effort to do yourself<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||01:53 PM||||I have to take that back. The caliper is $21 after you get your $10 core charge back. It includes the piston all installed, the bushings and seals for the hose, and the shiney new bleeder valve.<P>  Im almost hoping when I get done and bleed the front lines that the bleeder valve will break on the other side, so i will have an excuse to replace that caliper too!||||reg||1
